      "notes": "All three claims are well-supported by their quoted evidence. Tier assignments are correct (stated from M, measurable from parliamentary/institutional sources). The direction 'improves' is justified by the concrete loan charge commitment; the IR35 element is correctly treated as aspirational and not scored as a definite improvement. Magnitude 'minor' is appropriate given the limited affected population. The rationale is party-blind and does not impute motive. No lever leakage, no false balance issues \u2014 the verdict does not claim 'mixed' while evidence points one way. The McCann review reforms already in place (E6-E15) slightly complicate the baseline but the verdict acknowledges remaining liabilities are uncertain, which is handled appropriately in confidence and biggest_unknown. One minor observation: loanchargeappg.co.uk and hmrcloancharge.info are advocacy sources backing E3/E5, but the core claims are corroborated by commonslibrary.parliament.uk, so they are not the sole basis for any verdict."
